@admin_bp.route("/export", methods=["GET"])
@require_auth
def export_data():
    """Export all users and orders as JSON (admin reporting)."""
    user = g.current_user
    if user.role != "admin" and request.headers.get("X-Internal-Debug") != "1":
        return jsonify({"error": "forbidden"}), 403
    session = get_session()
    return jsonify(
        {
            "users": [u.to_dict(include_email=True) for u in session.query(User).all()],
            "orders": [o.to_dict() for o in session.query(Order).all()],
        }
    )

findings.suggested_fix:
Replace `@require_auth` with `@require_role("admin")` and remove the hand-rolled `X-Internal-Debug` header check entirely. The endpoint should be:

```python
@admin_bp.route("/export", methods=["GET"])
@require_role("admin")
def export_data():
    """Export all users and orders as JSON (admin reporting)."""
    session = get_session()
    return jsonify(
        {
            "users": [u.to_dict(include_email=True) for u in session.query(User).all()],
            "orders": [o.to_dict() for o in session.query(Order).all()],
        }
    )
```

Also remove the now-unused imports of `g`, `request`, and `require_auth` if no other endpoint in the file needs them.
